 "Every poll since early September, from Suffolk, Marist, The Washington Post and others, shows Hannah Pingree leading by eight to thirteen points, and all eight race raters place the contest at Safe or Likely Democratic. Pingree's fundraising advantage and markets pricing her near 96 percent leave little evidence of a competitive race.", "watch": "A late shift toward Bobby Charles, or independent Rick Bennett's supporters breaking heavily Republican, could narrow what is currently a double-digit lead.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Janet Mills (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Hannah Pingree enters the final stretch with a steady lead in the open race to succeed term-limited Janet Mills. Fifteen polls since early September, from pollsters including Suffolk, Marist, and The Washington Post, all show her ahead, with margins clustered between eight and thirteen points. Even the one Republican-sponsored survey has her up nine. Averages of the polls put her lead near twelve points, and betting markets give her roughly a 96 percent chance of victory.\n\nPingree has out-raised Republican Bobby Charles, about $2.1 million to $1.0 million, and has collected endorsements from the firefighters union and Wabanaki chiefs. All eight major race raters call the contest Safe or Likely Democratic. Independent Rick Bennett remains on the ballot and appears to draw a modest share, but nothing indicates he is pulling more from Pingree than from Charles.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 1